  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Life-Saving Nutrition Services for IDPs, Returnees, and Host Communities in WN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2025, a significant new influx of displaced families from North Kordofan arrived in the localities of Kosti, Rabak, Al Jabalain, and Tandalti. This additional wave of displacement has placed immense pressure on already overstretched services, limited food supplies, and fragile infrastructure, further worsening the humanitarian and nutrition situation for both IDPs and host communities.
Among the primary aims of the project is to rehabilitate and operationalise the Stabilisation Centre in Al-Gutaina and expand integrated CMAM, OTP, IYCF, and outreach services across Rabak, Al Jabalain, and Al-Gutaina, building on the achievements of the pilot project funded under CGF and GEF. The intervention will also strengthen community-level detection of malnutrition, integrate WASH and food security activities, and build resilience among both displaced and host populations.</narrative>
  </description>
